              "type": "text",
              "content": "angle of depression",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of a point on the object being viewed is the angle formed by the line of sight with the horizontal when the point is below the horizontal level, i.e., the case when we lower our head to look at the point being viewed (see Fig. 9.3)."
            }
